=base:summary.cmark
A root agent asks three helper agents at once, each runs its own tool, and a read-only dashboard shows all four sessions while they work. Recorded on a laptop with a local model, and reproducible from the repository.

=base:main-content.cmark

# See it work: four agents on one screen

One prompt, "Give me the tour.", goes to a front-desk agent. It asks three
helper agents in the same turn; each helper runs a command-line tool of its
own and reports back; the desk writes the answer. While that happens,
`agents-exe spectate` shows the four sessions and their tool calls live.

Everything on this page was recorded on 2026-10-03 from a build of `main`,
on a laptop, against a local model served by [Ollama](https://ollama.com/)
(`gemma4:e4b`). No hosted API and no real API key are involved, so you can
run the same thing; the agents are in
[`demo-agents/repo-tour/`](https://github.com/lucasdicioccio/agents-exe/tree/main/demo-agents/repo-tour).

## The screen, mid-run

The two frames below are unedited text captures of the `spectate` terminal
(100 columns by 24 rows), taken during one run.

1 minute 46 seconds in: the historian has returned, the code counter and
the librarian are still working. Each helper is a session of its own, listed
under the session that called it.

